Two <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> features need a little more time in testing and won't be shipping until a future update, even though they were present during the beta period.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/ios-27-passwords-auto-fix.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1052323" /><br/>
Suggestions in Messages conversations and the option to automatically fix compromised passwords with a tap will not be in the initial version of &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, and will instead launch in a later version of &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
Apple noted the delays <a href="https://www.apple.com/os/ios/">on its iOS 27 page</a>, as well as its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-27/">iPadOS 27</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a> pages as these are cross-platform features.<br/>
<br/>
For the password update feature, the Passwords app uses <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> and Safari to fix compromised passwords in the background without the user needing to do so manually<br/>
<br/>
In the Messages app, &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; surfaces one-tap suggestions based on what's being discussed in a conversation. If someone you're talking to asks you to send a photo or complete a task, Messages recognizes the request and suggests action on the information with the relevant apps.<br/>
<br/>
We already know that an iOS 27.1 update will be coming before October 23 because the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> comes out on that date and ships with it pre-installed. We could potentially get the new features as soon as iOS 27.1.<br/>
